# DURABLE REPRO — A2: a PROJECTION arg passed through a `Callable`-PARAM
# SEGFAULTS. Sibling of A1 (`sound_callable_amp_param_indirect_call.gg`), and a
# DISTINCT costume: A1 is a Callable-typed LOCAL bound to an `&`-param function;
# here the Callable arrives as a PARAMETER and the `&`-arg is a PROJECTION
# (`&c.fd`) rather than a whole local.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend): `gg check` reports "OK: no
# semantic errors", `gg build` succeeds, and the binary exits **139 (SIGSEGV)**.
# Reproduces at base AND under the `&`-of-projection prototype, so the
# projection fix does not close it.
#
# ⚠ `gg run` MASKS this as exit 1 with no output — it does not propagate the
# child's signal status. Reproduce by BUILDING and running the binary directly,
# or the failure looks like an ordinary build error.
#
# ROOT (measured, not inferred): there are THREE indirect-call argument loops,
# not one. `calls.rs:1395-1399` (`__Closure_N__call`) routes through
# `lower_call_arg` and therefore honours `arg.node.ownership`; but
# `calls.rs:1455` and `calls.rs:1880` (FnPtr / `__gorget_closure_call_N`) call
# `lower_expr(&arg.node.value)` DIRECTLY and ignore the sigil entirely. The SEGV
# takes one of the two non-routing paths — so this is a MISSING SIGIL CHECK, not
# an ABI or codegen defect.
#
# INTENDED: the indirect call is an ordinary write-through call, so `bumpret`
# increments the caller's `c.fd` and the program prints 11 then 11 and exits 0.
# (If the language instead decides an `&`-param function may not be reified into
# a `Callable` value, the reference-grade answer is a CHECK-TIME rejection —
# never an accepted program that segfaults. Either way today's behaviour is a
# defect; this fixture asserts the accept-and-run reading, matching its A1
# sibling and the `Callable[int(&int)]` annotation the compiler already accepts.)
#
# ORACLE (ggdef): OUT OF SUBSET — ggdef does not reify a named function into a
# `Callable` value ("unresolved local"). Recorded explicitly per Core #9.
#
# The seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so no const-fold can elide the call.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): "A PROJECTION arg through a
# `Callable`-PARAM segfaults".

struct Counter:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

int bumpret(int &n):
    n = n + 1
    return n

int with_it(Callable[int(&int)] f, Counter &c):
    return f(&c.fd)

void main():
    Counter c = Counter(seed())
    print(with_it(bumpret, &c))
    print(c.fd)
